WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:05.080
When a hyper-aggressive lizard or an evil,
living cow-heart starts rampaging through

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.560
your town, or a sinister salesman turns up
in your home, who you gonna call?

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.430
Hint, it’s not the Ghostbusters.

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:15.110
The answer is… the SCP Foundation’s Mobile
Task Force.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:18.770
You’ve probably heard them mentioned in
every single video on this channel, but what

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:20.930
exactly is a Mobile Task Force?

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:25.040
What do they do for the SCP Foundation and
what are some of the most famous Mobile Task

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.080
Forces in the field?

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.710
Let’s crack open the files and take a look!

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:33.690
In short, Mobile Task Forces are the Foundation’s
elite personnel, and each task force is generally

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:37.800
made up of highly-trained Foundation operatives
with specific skill sets.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.399
These MTFs aren’t rooted to any one base,
and are relocated to wherever they’re required

00:00:42.399 --> 00:00:44.780
– hence the “Mobile” part of their name.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:48.890
The exact parameters of what an MTF can be
is pretty flexible – the size of their units

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:53.950
can vary from whole battalions of troops packing
heavy artillery to smale, tight-knit groups

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:56.050
of intelligence-gathering spies.

00:00:56.050 --> 00:01:01.240
Some Mobile Task Forces are bound to specific
SCPs, whereas others perform more generalized

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.610
tasks, such as securing certain facilities
or territories.

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:08.609
When the regular rank and file Foundation
Field Agents can’t do the job, the MTFs

00:01:08.609 --> 00:01:10.679
are brought in to pick up the pieces.

00:01:10.679 --> 00:01:14.610
Each group is controlled by a Mobile Task
Force Commander, who reports to the Foundation

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:19.479
Director of Task Forces, though the actual
organizational structure of each group varies.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:24.369
Sometimes, MTFs which were created for extremely
specific purposes are disbanded after that

00:01:24.369 --> 00:01:25.369
purpose is achieved.

00:01:25.369 --> 00:01:28.289
How many Mobile Task Forces are there, exactly?

00:01:28.289 --> 00:01:32.890
The exact number is shrouded in secrecy, and
oftentimes the answer will depend on who you

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:33.890
ask.

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:35.860
But you’re not here for what we don’t
know.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:39.819
You want to know the details on the biggest
badasses under the Foundation’s employ,

00:01:39.819 --> 00:01:41.399
and we intend to deliver.

00:01:41.399 --> 00:01:45.799
Much like our video on the proposals for SCP
– 001, we’re going to give you a rapid

00:01:45.799 --> 00:01:50.540
fire crash-course on some of the most prominent
and interesting Foundation task forces.

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:54.469
And remember, if you want us to go more in
depth into the most exciting missions of any

00:01:54.469 --> 00:01:56.479
of these groups, let us know in the comments!

00:01:56.479 --> 00:02:00.859
But for now, it’s time for a rundown of
the Foundation’s best of the best.

00:02:00.859 --> 00:02:07.069
MTF Alpha-1, aka "Red Right Hand", are essentially
the Black Ops of the SCP Foundation.

00:02:07.069 --> 00:02:11.750
They report directly to the O5 Council and
conduct missions at the highest level of secrecy

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:15.920
– with most of the information hidden behind
a Level 5 clearance wall.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:20.420
Many also believe Alpha-1 to have a link to
the infamous Chaos Insurgency – a splinter

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:24.740
group at war with the Foundation – but if
anyone asks, you didn’t hear it from us.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:26.670
Seriously, we don’t want to get assassinated.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:33.050
MTF Alpha-4, aka "Pony Express", are a covert
group deeply embedded in the world’s logistics

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:34.420
and postal services.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:38.520
The trafficking of anomalous objects is a
worldwide issue, and it’s up to Alpha-4

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:43.320
to intercept and keep a lid on these anomalous
objects before they fall into the wrong hands.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:47.620
Think of them as a better-funded, paranormal
USPS Police Division.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:52.490
One object they’ve prevented from reaching
the public is SCP - 3060, a series of CPAP

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:55.900
Machines that cause nighttime visions of frightening
entities.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:03:01.680
MTF Omega-7, aka "Pandora's Box", was an experimental
task force which incorporated the use of highly

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:07.120
combat-effective SCPs – including SCP – 076,
better known as Abel.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.250
The test showed initial success but after
they ran out of missions, Abel’s bloodlust

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:15.690
proved to be too great for the team to control
and the experiment as well as the task force

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:16.690
were scrapped.

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:21.920
However, this led to the creation of…
MTF Alpha-9, aka "Last Hope."

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:26.980
This is a mobile task force designed to train
viable SCPs to provide services to the Foundation

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:27.980
out in the field.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:31.750
This group has learned the lessons of its
predecessor and has employed the use of more

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:34.030
measured and reasonable anomalies.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:39.490
Those include SCP – 073, or Cain, the much-more
even-tempered brother of Able.

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:45.280
MTF Beta-7, aka the "Maz Hatters", are the
elite clean-up crew for anomalous biohazards,

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.510
chemical spills, and radiological disasters.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:51.390
So, if an area suddenly looks like it’s
going to become Chernobyl’s scarier sequel,

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:56.720
or an anomalous, fast-spreading disease is
wreaking havoc over a wide area, the Maz Hatters

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:01.980
are the guys to call.They worked closely on
the containment of SCP - 1280, a kind of parasitic

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:05.720
nematode worm that often inject false memories
into their victims.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:11.070
MTF Gamma-5, aka "Red Herrings", are the Foundation’s
chief disinformation division.

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:14.870
They prevent the leaks of classified information
to the public, and on the rare occasions that

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:19.090
this information does somehow get out, they’re
in charge of burying it and administering

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:21.680
necessary amnestic treatment to those affected.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:25.319
It’s a thankless job, but you won’t remember
they did it, either way.

00:04:25.319 --> 00:04:30.620
They gave amnestic treatment to the traumatized
victims of SCP - 1618, a malevolent urinal

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:34.800
which replaces the user’s valuables with
disgusting alternatives, from toilet paper

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.099
to pig intestines.

00:04:36.099 --> 00:04:42.139
MTF Gamma-6, aka "Deep Feeders", investigate
and track deep sea or oceanic anomalies – a

00:04:42.139 --> 00:04:46.509
job that commands the ultimate respect from
people with thalassophobia, that’s the fear

00:04:46.509 --> 00:04:47.740
of the deep ocean.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:51.270
If something terrifying and mysterious is
stirring down there in the abyss, you better

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.710
believe Gamma-6 are gonna be the first ones
down.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:59.490
They keep a close eye on a number of anomalies,
such as SCP - 1264, an underwater amalgamation

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:04.229
of sunken ships, eager to drag down more vessels
and add them to its mass.

00:05:04.229 --> 00:05:10.500
MTF Gamma-13, aka "Asimov's Lawbringers",
are a specialized task force devoted to investigating,

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:15.110
tracking, and apprehending anomalies originating
from Anderson Robotics, a group of interest

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:17.879
that produces anomalous robots and machines.

00:05:17.879 --> 00:05:23.669
This includes examples of SCP - 2806, a number
of advanced, anomalous prosthetic body parts

00:05:23.669 --> 00:05:27.919
that wish to attach themselves to a lacking
host - whether they want it or not.

00:05:27.919 --> 00:05:33.509
MTF Delta-5, aka "Front Runners", are a large
group of autonomous deep-cover agents buried

00:05:33.509 --> 00:05:35.930
in various Groups of Interest across the globe.

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:40.110
It’s their job to gather intelligence from
within to aid in the apprehension of anomalies

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:42.569
before these groups can get their hands on
them.

00:05:42.569 --> 00:05:47.099
They also sometimes make use of anomalies
to track down others, such as when they requested

00:05:47.099 --> 00:05:53.419
to use SCP - 185, a Russian R-105M radio used
during the Cold War that can receive signals

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:58.449
from any time period including encrypted ones,
but can also emit sound waves so powerful

00:05:58.449 --> 00:06:00.249
they can literally kill you.

00:06:00.249 --> 00:06:05.339
MTF Epsilon-9, aka "Fire Eaters", are the
Foundation’s resident pyromaniacs.

00:06:05.339 --> 00:06:09.069
They’re the ones sent into missions involving
extremely high-temperature environments, and

00:06:09.069 --> 00:06:13.469
they’re also highly skilled in the use of
powerful incendiary weapons.

00:06:13.469 --> 00:06:17.900
If the Foundation needs to burn or avoid getting
burned, the Fire Eaters are the ones for the

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:18.900
job.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:24.029
Their vital skills assisted in containing
SCP - 165, massive colonies of carnivorous,

00:06:24.029 --> 00:06:26.860
parasitic mites that eat prey to the bone.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:32.759
MTF Epsilon-11, "Nine-Tailed Fox", are another
one of the most classified Mobile Task Forces,

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:35.449
existing only under the oversight of Red Right
Hand.

00:06:35.449 --> 00:06:39.469
They work internally, and are only dispatched
to Foundation sites when standard protocols

00:06:39.469 --> 00:06:41.960
fail and multiple breaches are imminent.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:47.280
They were brought in to deal with the SCP
- 2139 incident, a strange psychological phenomenon

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:52.300
that inexplicably increased the suggestibility
of Foundation staff at Site - 35.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:55.460
This made the infected staff agree with everything
they heard.

00:06:55.460 --> 00:07:00.819
MTF Zeta-9, "Mole Rats", are a task force
that specializes in the exploration and containment

00:07:00.819 --> 00:07:05.500
of anomalous areas that are either enclosed
or underground – particularly if, due to

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:09.930
the effects of the anomaly, the spacetime
fabric of the area is unstable.

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:14.879
You may remember them from our series on SCP
– 1730: The mission into and out of the

00:07:14.879 --> 00:07:15.990
anomalous Site 13.

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:22.180
MTF Eta-10, aka "See No Evil", are a team
that specializes in taking on dangerous memes

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:25.729
and cognitohazards that affect the victims
through visual contact.

00:07:25.729 --> 00:07:30.900
One example is SCP - 1561, a crown that, when
worn, causes all those who see the person

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:35.460
wearing the crown to imagine the wearer as
their king - and immediately adopt positions

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:36.460
of servitude.

00:07:36.460 --> 00:07:40.749
While MTF Eta-11, aka "Savage Beasts", serve
the opposite purpose.

00:07:40.749 --> 00:07:44.999
They deal with musical or auditory anomalies,
and any cognitohazards that work through the

00:07:44.999 --> 00:07:50.969
medium of sound, like SCP - 2402, a chord
progression which can regenerate old or dying

00:07:50.969 --> 00:07:51.969
cells.

00:07:51.969 --> 00:07:56.899
MTF Theta-4, aka "Gardeners", are a crack
team of agents who face off against any botanical

00:07:56.899 --> 00:07:58.509
or plant-like anomalies.

00:07:58.509 --> 00:08:03.449
Their skills were put to use against SCP - 1147,
a collection of plum tree seeds which can

00:08:03.449 --> 00:08:07.340
grow out of literally any substance - even
ones that are totally inorganic.

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:13.029
MTF Theta-90, aka "Angle Grinders", are a
team that specialize in the two most frightening

00:08:13.029 --> 00:08:16.189
things out there: Anomalies, and math.

00:08:16.189 --> 00:08:21.699
These brainiacs deal with anomalous mathematical
issues like warped topologies and geometries.

00:08:21.699 --> 00:08:25.999
Even listing an example of the kind of anomalies
they deal with here will make your head hurt,

00:08:25.999 --> 00:08:27.689
so just be thankful they’re out there.

00:08:27.689 --> 00:08:33.140
MTF Iota-10, "Damn Feds", are a huge network
of undercover agents based in federal and

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:35.650
local law enforcement agencies across the
globe.

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:39.840
They intercept any anomalous objects, beings,
or information, and make sure that it makes

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:44.130
its way out of police evidence lockers and
into Foundation hands without incident.

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:50.520
MTF Kappa-10, "Skynet", is a temporary team
of combined meatspace and virtual agents tracking

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:56.250
down and disrupting anomalous cyber-threats,
such as SCP - 2987, an external hard drive

00:08:56.250 --> 00:09:02.000
basically capable of turning artificial intelligences
into living souls for trades with soul-consuming

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.000
anomalies.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:08.340
MTF Lambda-5, aka "White Rabbits", are a group
that specializes in combating reality warpers

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:12.960
of all types, whether they’re messing with
spacetime or exhibiting godlike powers.

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:18.830
Some anomalies even respond directly to them,
like SCP - 2446 - a phenomenon where corpses,

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:23.350
often identical to living White Rabbits team
members, suddenly manifest around San Jose,

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:24.350
California.

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:29.300
MTF Lambda-12, "Pest Control", are a group
of agents who exclusively go after anomalous

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:30.300
vermin.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:33.511
Incidentally, they’re one of the only MTFs
who’ve never lost members in the line of

00:09:33.511 --> 00:09:34.511
duty.

00:09:34.511 --> 00:09:39.000
Their purview includes SCP - 2810, an anomalous
pathogen that causes the victim’s cells

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:43.450
to become tiny versions of their own species
- like a human’s cells becoming cell-sized

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:44.450
humans.

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:49.680
MTF Lambda-14, "One Star Reviewers", are a
Task Force that deals with retail-oriented

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:50.680
anomalies.

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:55.020
Their main focus has become combating a sinister
group of interest known as The Ambrose Restaurant

00:09:55.020 --> 00:10:00.070
- a chain of extradimensional restaurants
with strange and anomalous food and service.

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:04.750
MTF Mu-3, aka "Highest Bidders", is a mobile
task force devoted to preventing the Group

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:09.020
of Interest “Marshall, Carter, and Dark
Ltd.” from disseminating dangerous, anomalous

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:12.260
objects, and then obtaining and containing
these objects.

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:17.950
One such object is SCP - 2818, a number of
50 Cal sniper rifles that, when fired, turns

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:20.810
the shooter into a bullet and fires them.

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:26.470
MTF Mu-4, aka "Debuggers", are particularly
useful in the modern age, as they track and

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:31.090
contain anomalous electronics and technology
– including isolating and containing anomalous

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:32.440
websites and software.

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:38.200
One of the anomalies dealt with by the Debuggers
is SCP - 896, an online role playing game

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:42.410
that improves the physical and mental attributes
of the player when they name their character

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.000
after themselves.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:46.380
Remember when we said you didn’t need to
call the Ghostbusters?

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:48.780
Well that wasn’t entirely true.

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:55.140
Sometimes you need to get MTF Mu-13, aka "Ghostbusters"
on the line since they are an MTF whose specialty

00:10:55.140 --> 00:11:01.610
is tracking intangible or incorporeal anomalies,
particularly those considered sapient or sentient,

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:05.890
and they’re on call 24 hours a day to serve
all your supernatural containment needs, like

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:11.490
when you’re plagued by SCP - 1036, which
a number of haunted Kongolese fetish dolls.

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:17.390
MTF Nu-7, aka "Hammer Down", are the ones
you call when you need real heavy-duty work.

00:11:17.390 --> 00:11:21.880
They’re a huge force with a massive stock
of army vehicles and heavy weaponry and are

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:24.440
only called in for truly catastrophic events.

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:30.240
They also assisted in the containment of SCP
- 939, the voice-imitating, amnestic-producing

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:31.370
red monsters.

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:36.470
MTF Epsilon-6, aka "Village Idiots", are a
group of agents whose specialty is investigating

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:40.600
and containing anomalous phenomena that occur
in rural or suburban areas.

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:44.540
If you live in a small town and you’re on
the run from a vicious monster, you better

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:46.720
hope the Village Idiots are on their way.

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:52.340
They contained SCP - 2561, a cat with a vintage
television set for a head, capable of causing

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:53.420
painful tinnitus.

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:59.280
MTF Pi-1, aka "City Slickers", are pretty
much the exact opposite of the village idiots.

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:03.600
They pursue anomalies in densely populated
urban areas, particularly in the New York

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:04.850
metropolitan area.

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:10.920
They assisted in the ongoing containment of
SCP - 1155, the incredibly bloodthirsty Predatory

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:12.030
Street Art.

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:18.310
MTF Sigma-66, aka "Sixteen Tons", are basically
the Foundation’s own version of the Suicide

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:19.310
Squad.

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:23.160
They’re a team made from captured members
of other groups of interest who aren’t particularly

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:27.820
loyal to the Foundation, but whose very particular
set of skills make up for that fact.

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:34.690
MTF Tau-5, aka "Samsara", are another group
you may remember from the events of SCP – 1730.

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:39.590
These are a group unlike any other – immortal
cyborgs made from the flesh of a dead god,

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:41.480
who can be upgraded as needed.

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:47.760
They’re equipped with experimental and state
of the art Foundation technology to take on

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:49.500
thaumaturgic, magical, and psionic threats.

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:54.000
MTF Psi-7, aka "Home Improvement", is a team
specializing in structural anomalies.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:58.930
In plain speak, they deal with anomalous activities
concerning buildings, containing and sometimes

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:02.710
even demolishing when necessary with a variety
of heavy artillery.

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:07.670
For example, they counteract the nightmarish
SCP - 3050 - a building in North Carolina

00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:12.680
that, once a year, fuses all living matter
inside into its own structure on an atomic

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:13.680
level.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:19.010
MTF Psi-8, aka "The Silencers", are a team
devoted to containing reanimation anomalies

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:20.860
and those who’ve been affected by them.

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:24.260
If you’ve just come back from the dead,
then The Silencers are going to want to know

00:13:24.260 --> 00:13:25.360
your location.

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:31.010
MTF Omega-0, aka "Ará Orún", are another
highly classified mobile task force that is

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:35.730
actually the memories of deceased Foundation
personnel preserved on the Foundation Intranet

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:36.730
system.

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:40.990
Their job is to protect their surviving co-workers
against informational threats on the servers.

00:13:40.990 --> 00:13:46.900
They also contain SCP - 3664, a damaged but
highly advanced assault rifle existing in

00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:51.150
the non-physical, conceptual space - It can
only be interacted with by thinking about

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:52.440
interacting with it.

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:58.080
And last but not least, MTF Omega-12, aka
"Achilles' Heels", is also an anomalous task

00:13:58.080 --> 00:13:59.080
force.

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:03.100
These powerful reality warpers from another
dimension hunt down dangerous and powerful

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:04.910
reality warpers in ours.

00:14:04.910 --> 00:14:08.920
You can thank these guys for every single
day that our reality continues on as normal

00:14:08.920 --> 00:14:11.240
– or whatever “normal” means now.

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:16.750
They’re enemies of SCP - 3155, members of
the iconic Pinkerton Detective Agency with

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:19.040
anomalous abilities relating to combat.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:20.820
Alright, we did it!

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:25.470
Of course, even this is only a sample of the
vast number of Mobile Task Forces at the Foundation’s

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:30.030
disposal who put their lives at risk every
day to keep humanity, normality, and reality

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:31.030
intact.

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:35.020
